rebecca: quick note from QA: streaming+paginator snippets still show naive whole-page retry. the gateway now supports mid-page resume via X-Resume-Token. we need a short, copy-pasteable shim for py/ts/go showing resume_token + bounded retries. keep it tiny and clear.
owen: i can do TS. will provide an async iterator helper and a small retry wrapper.
sana: i'll take Python and add a tiny helper function that other docs can import. also update the Streaming guide paragraph.
eli: i'll do Go and add a one-paragraph compatibility note for RELEASE_NOTES.
rebecca: TS draft (sdk-style):
```ts
// resumable iterator + bounded retry helper (TS SDK pseudo)
async function drainResumable(path) {
  const iter = client.streamPaginate(path)
  let lastToken = undefined
  for await (const page of iter) {
    for (const c of page.chunks) process.stdout.write(c.text)
    const t = page.headers['x-resume-token']
    if (t) { lastToken = t; iter.resume(t) }
  }
}
```
sana: Python draft (docs helper):
```python
# docs helper: bounded resume attempts
from time import sleep

def drain_with_resume(client, path, attempts=5):
    resume = None
    for _ in range(attempts):
        resp = client.stream_paginate(path, resume_token=resume)
        for p in resp.pages():
            for c in p.chunks: print(c.text, end='')
        resume = resp.headers.get('x-resume-token')
        if not resume:
            return
        sleep(min(3, 0.2 * (2 ** _)))
    raise RuntimeError('resume attempts exhausted')
```
eli: Go pseudo (compact):
```go
req := client.NewPaginateReq("/v1/huge")
back := NewBackoff(200*time.Millisecond, 3*time.Second, true)
for {
  resp, err := client.StreamPaginate(ctx, req)
  if err != nil { time.Sleep(back.Next()); continue }
  io.Copy(os.Stdout, resp.Body)
  if tok := resp.Header.Get("X-Resume-Token"); tok != "" { req.ResumeToken = tok; continue }
  break
}
```
rebecca: docs blurb suggestion: "Servers may truncate long streaming responses under load. When present, X-Resume-Token allows clients to resume inside a logical page. Clients should prefer server-provided resume tokens and perform bounded, jittered retries (base=200ms, max=3s, attempts=5). Avoid re-requesting the whole page." 
